                <head>Annex 4</head>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Supplementary Note</hi>
                </p>
                <p>In the course of discussions between representatives of the United States and the
                    United Kingdom on the subject of the exchange and/or disclosure of classified
                    military information on January 23, 1950, the representatives of the United
                    Kingdom requested that the following statement be placed in the record:</p>
                <p>The representatives of the Government of the United Kingdom wish to place on
                    record that they consider it most essential that the C.M.I.B. procedure should
                    be expeditious in operation and should take account of factors wider than
                    security alone. This should be made clear in the directives addressed by each
                    Government to their representatives on the Board.</p>
            </div>
